  "body": {
    "id": "thm:unequal-three-arm-sharp-limit",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For \\(c^\\dagger=(1,-1/4,-3/4)\\), \\[\\liminf_{n\\to\\infty}n^{4/3}\\{n^{-1}-R_n(c^\\dagger)\\}\\ge\\Lambda_{c^\\dagger}=C_A(5/8)^{2/3}>0.\\] This one-sided attaining result does not assert existence of the limit or a matching all-design converse.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "c^\\dagger",
      "n",
      "R_n(c)",
      "\\Lambda_c",
      "C_A"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:risk-game",
      "prop:unequal-three-arm-exact-primitives",
      "def:airy-benchmark",
      "thm:qstar-uniform-risk-upper"
    ],
    "justification": "This short consequence converts the local orbit saddle into the sharp unrestricted decision value at the designated unequal contrast.",
    "gap": "The accepted parent's rate and subsequential certificate results do not imply convergence or identify a constant at \\(c^\\dagger\\).",
    "consumer": "It gives a sharp worst-case precision benchmark for a fixed-horizon three-regimen trial using the \\(1:-1/4:-3/4\\) contrast.",
    "proof_tex": "The exact-primitives proposition proves \\(\\kappa(c^\\dagger)=5/8\\).  The Airy-benchmark definition therefore gives\n\\[\n \\Lambda_{c^\\dagger}=C_A\\kappa(c^\\dagger)^{2/3}\n =C_A(5/8)^{2/3}>0,\n\\tag{14}\n\\]\nwhere positivity uses the declared range \\(C_A\\in(0,\\infty)\\).  Applying the established uniform-risk upper theorem to the permitted three-active-arm contrast \\(c^\\dagger\\) gives\n\\[\n \\liminf_{n\\to\\infty}n^{4/3}\n \\{n^{-1}-R_n(c^\\dagger)\\}\n \\ge \\Lambda_{c^\\dagger}.\n\\tag{15}\n\\]\nCombining (14) and (15) proves the narrowed statement.  This argument is attaining-side only: it supplies no reverse inequality, and the exact contradiction (12)--(13) prevents the proposed widening tube from supplying one.",
